  set:  # c26d
    title: "swift: 622 untyped receivers carry a NAME that _type_of cannot resolve (27.1% of classified untyped sites on vapor; more hide in the WI-sulas chain bucket)"  # c26d
    description: "FILED 2026-09-10 from WI-dodop (PR #877 / measurement 0028). Instrument:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dodop_swift_09102026/untyped.py (receiver_type_hint\nabsent on a call_construct=method edge; multi-call lines dropped, 25% cap).\n\nMEASURED, vapor @ ff88583, re-run 2026-09-30 on dev 134a06d505 (output:\n~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/dryrun_09302026/C/swift_untyped.out). 5,243 method\nedges, typed 1,885 (36.0%), untyped 3,358; 2,295 sites classified, 559 on\nmulti-call lines dropped (19.6%):\n\n    923  40.2%  chain off a simple_identifier head: v.p.m()\n    622  27.1%  receiver_hint PRESENT, `_type_of` RAN and returned None   <- THIS\n    435  19.0%  self.<method>()                         -- WI-sizas\n    166   7.2%  chain off a navigation_expression\n     56   2.4%  self.<property>.<method>()              -- fixed by PR #877\n    ~93         literals, call() result, tuples, super, ...\n\nThe 923-site chain bucket exists because b4fc27e0c7 (WI-sulas) stopped typing a\n2+-hop chain v.p.m() by its head v: those sites used to carry hint=v and count\nhere. So this item's population is the 622 single-hop sites PLUS whatever part\nof the 923 has a head `_type_of` cannot type either -- that part has not been\ncounted.\n\nWHAT IT IS. `x.method()` where `x` is a lowercase simple_identifier -- a local, a\nparameter, or an implicit-self property -- and swift's `_type_of` cannot name its\ntype. `_type_of` consults, in order: `_scoped_types` (per enclosing function,\ninnermost first), `var_types`, then `_inherited_field_type`. The binding pass\nfills them from a property_declaration (its annotation, else the callee's return\ntype through the return-type registry), an `if let` / `guard let` binding, and a\nparameter. There is NO arm for a closure parameter (vapor example:\n`ws.onText { ws, string in ...}`), a tuple destructuring, or an `if case let`\nbinding; which of these, or a missing return-type row, accounts for the 622 is\nnot yet known -- that is the first step, not a fix.\n\nDO NOT ASSUME IT IS ONE CAUSE. WI-dodop's own history is a headline that pooled\npopulations twice (16.5% pooled slot-filled with correctly-refused; the untyped\n2,832 pooled hint-absent with hint-present). Size the 622 by WHY `_type_of`\nfailed before designing anything: no declaration in scope, a declaration whose\ntype annotation is absent and whose callee has no registry row, a closure\nparameter, a tuple destructuring, an `if case let` binding.\n\nPRICE ON THE MODULE SLOT, NEVER THE TYPED SHARE. A PROJECT type is typed and then\ncorrectly REFUSED (INV-kotob), so the share moves where the slot does not; on\nthis same corpus the share rose 368 where the slot rose 252. And a filled slot is\nnecessary, not sufficient (L5): measurement 0025 moved 787 correct objc names and\nrecall by ZERO, so the acceptance number is PRIMITIVES REACHED.\n\nDIRECTION WARNING: more typed receivers feed sanitizer registration and a\nregistered barrier earns `sanitized` and DROPS a flow (ADR-0052 recorded that the\nescape-closing family's only reachable effect on findings today is suppression).\nMeasure at L4 in BOTH directions.\n\nRelated: WI-sizas (self.<method>), WI-janad (`any P` annotations), INV-bisok\n(Alamofire Session not extracted).\n\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # c26d
- op: discuss  # 84f3
  at: '2026-10-01T11:29:42Z'  # 84f3
  by: agent  # 84f3
