  clock: 4  # 84f3
  nonce: 84f3  # 84f3
  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-01 (concurrent run; local branch, NOT pushed). Branch jgstern-agent/fix/mofil-swift-named-receiver-binding-forms in ~/hg_wt/mofil, commit a7d20798f2 on origin/dev 8cfcab7b07. Status unchanged (owner closes).\n\nSTEP 1 -- THE 622 SIZED BY CAUSE (the item's first ask). Instrument: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/decontend/run_09302026/mofil/causes.py -- the item's untyped.py population (call_construct=method, no receiver_type_hint, single-call lines, lowercase hint, _type_of None), each receiver NAME looked up by an upward scope walk in its own file and classified by the first binding found. Reproduces 622 on vapor @ ff88583 (2,295 classified, 559 multi-call dropped = 19.6%). vapor causes:\n  115 closure parameter, UNANNOTATED (ws.onText { ws, s in })\n   87 local = method call, no return-type row, expression receiver\n   70 SUBSCRIPT parsed as a method call (x.p[i]) -- not a method call at all\n   56 closure shorthand $0\n   56 local annotated [T] (array; refused by design, WI-bodav's family)\n   52+23 local = method call, no return-type row (named / capitalised receiver)\n   23 not declared in this file (cross-file field/global)\n   22 local = GENERIC constructor T<A>(...)  (constructor_expression)\n   20+2 case-let / if-case payload\n   16 file-level string literal; 12 local = navigation_expression; 7 for-in; 5 newValue; 4 tuple; ... (full tables: causes.<repo>.before.out)\nSame instrument on hummingbird (B=1,120: closure-unannotated 462, subscript 160, generic ctor 88, tuple 72, ANNOTATED closure param 34), Kingfisher (542: bare lowercase call 159 = XCTest expectation(description:)), Alamofire (1,190: bare lowercase call 718 = XCTest expectation), swift-argument-parser (281). NOT one cause, as the item warned.\n\nSTEP 2 -- WHAT THE BRANCH CHANGES (swift.py binding pass + emit lookup; TDD, 26 tests in test_swift_named_receiver_binding_forms.py, red on origin/dev first):\n  (a) optional-binding conditions bind EVERY let/var clause; a clause annotation names the type; while-let binds. The old arm took the condition's first identifier and first '=': `if flag, let s = f()` stamped f()'s type on `flag` (observed: swift:URLSession:0-0:fileExists on a Bool), a second clause never bound, `if case let .some(x)` bound the case name `some`.\n  (b) generic constructor T<A>(...) names T; (c) identifier initialiser copies the type; (d) annotated closure parameter binds.\n  The A/B then showed three scope-map defects these arms made bite, fixed in the same mechanism: (e) a scoped binding is visible only from the END of its declaration (a later local retyped a field use above it: hummingbird URLEncodedFormDecoder.swift:269 stamped KDC); (f) every callable body is a scope -- closure, init, deinit, subscript, getter/setter/willSet/didSet -- not only func (init params and accessor locals had landed in the FILE-level map: Alamofire init(..., downstream: Downstream) typed the field `downstream: Protected<Downstream?>` as Downstream at 12 sites; a computed property's local typed every `router` in hummingbird ApplicationTests.swift); (g) the in-repo bind looks a generic receiver type up by its bare name (Result<Success, Failure>.tryMap -> Result.tryMap).\n\nSTEP 3 -- MEASURED (analyze_swift A/B, 5 repos, origin/dev swift.py vs branch; arm.py/diff.py/readback.py in the run dir). `calls` edge totals identical in every repo. Module slot (external method edges, dst module != external): vapor 1038->1068, hummingbird 790->816, Kingfisher 897->912, Alamofire 488->489, swift-argument-parser 151->153. Per module, vapor: ManagedAtomic +21, Channel +3, NIOLockedValueBox +2, EventLoopFuture +2. BUT part of the gain is a pre-existing slot leak (filed WI-jofin): hummingbird URLEncodedFormNode.Array +19, Kingfisher DiskStorage.Backend +5, Alamofire URLEncodedFormEncoder.* +9 are PROJECT nested types; vapor C +1 is a generic parameter; hummingbird Bool +2 is WRONG (overload collapse, filed WI-hubik). Alamofire's net +1 is -12 Downstream (a generic-param name, removed) plus +13. Unresolved method edges newly bound in-repo: 6/176/24/116/15; 30 sampled, every one read on its line, 6 declarations opened, all correct. Edges that LOST a type or resolution: 3/14/5/12/1 -- every one opened came from a name-keyed or file-level LEAK, wrong (Alamofire downstream/request/dateEncoding, Kingfisher CGImageSource, sap Element) or right only by coincidence (Kingfisher alert, hummingbird router/source/node).\nNOT MEASURED: io-boundary primitives reached / chains (L5) -- queued, see the report; taint/sanitizer direction (no claims file run). The typed SHARE is not the unit and is not reported as one.\n\nTESTS: smart-test targeted (298 files), 9,273 passed, 0 failed, 1 xfailed; 100% coverage on changed files; mypy strict ratchet 513 = baseline. module_key_axis.py's two swift.py EmissionSite pins relocated by anchor (1895->1994, 1966->2065).\n\nFILED: WI-dimad (subscript parsed as a call -> phantom resolved edges, P2), WI-zobif (unannotated closure params need the callee's closure signature, P3), WI-silos (untyped declarations do not shadow; blocks are not scopes, P3), WI-hubik (return-type registry collapses overloads, P3), WI-rajig (tuple / case-let payload / newValue bindings, P3), WI-jofin (generic params and nested project types fill the module slot, P3). NOT filed: Alamofire/Kingfisher's largest bucket, `let exp = expectation(description:)` -- a bare call to an inherited XCTest method; its receivers (fulfill/wait) reach no io row, recorded here only."  # 84f3
